<title>USA: Top Latin companies boost sales in 1996 - report.</title>
<headline>Top Latin companies boost sales in 1996 - report.</headline>
<dateline>MIAMI 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Most of Latin America's top publicly traded companies boosted sales and net income last year, Latin Trade magazine says in its September issue.</p>
<p>In a survey of the Miami-based magazine's Top 100 companies made available Thursday, 73 showed growth in sales. Total sales increased by 11.3 percent to a combined $228.1 billion. Net income grew by 40.9 percent to $21.4 billion, it said.</p>
<p>Brazil dominated the list with 49 entries. Its oil giant Petrobas kept the top spot, increasing sales by 7 percent.</p>
<p>Mexico was in second place with 30 companies, followed by Argentina with 11.</p>
<p>Steel, electricity and beverage companies posted mixed results for last year while the retail and telecommunications sectors showed the strongest growth.</p>
<p>The list had 16 newcomers, among them Brazilian construction giant Odebrecht, Chile's Luksic group, Argentina's Banco de Galicia y Buenos Aires and Venezuelan telecommunications company CANTV.</p>
